eczos-windows-core (0.1.0~dev9) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Run installers from the isolated Windows C: drive.
  * Add a visible ECZ Windows application manager and failed-install retry.
  * Detect a missing 32-bit Wine runtime before creating an application.
  * Start Wine inside C: so self-extracting installers receive a valid working
    directory after the unsafe Z: mapping is removed.
  * Prevent concurrent installation attempts for one application record.
  * Prefer Windows Start Menu shortcuts for application discovery and support
    rescanning completed installations.
  * Keep Wine background processes from inheriting the installation lock.
  * Launch Start Menu shortcuts through their internal C: path without Z:.
  * Resolve verified executable targets from Windows shortcut metadata.
  * Add explicit per-application Windows drive mappings without restoring Z:.

